# Hub API contract

Canonical API surface: [`openapi/openapi.yaml`](openapi/openapi.yaml).

When adding or changing HTTP endpoints, update that OpenAPI file in the same change as `crates/api/src/routes.rs`.

Clients (web, Afterglow) must match this contract — especially:

- `GET /api/v1/catalog/search` and `/browse` return `CatalogPage` (`items`, `page`, `total_pages`, `rows`, `has_more`) — not a bare array
- `GET /api/v1/catalog/preview` returns overview + gallery (`CatalogPreview`) without adding to the library
- `PATCH /api/v1/games/{id}` — `user_rating`: omit = unchanged, `null` = clear, number = set
- Prefer screenshot `cached_url` (`/api/v1/media/...`) over F95 `full_url`
- `POST /api/v1/games/{id}/refresh` registers stubs then awaits screenshot cache (~120s); timeout continues in background
- Screenshot galleries keep the full F95 URL list (stubs) even when only a subset is hub-cached yet
- `GET /api/v1/settings/f95/cookies` exports the stored F95 cookie header for desktop browser handoff
- Download links: `label` = platform; `title` = pack/section heading (episode, version, etc.) when present above hoster clusters
- `POST /api/v1/library/add` accepts optional `title_hint` (Browse should send the card title); full thread URLs also yield a slug-derived SAM hint. Numeric-id search alone often misses.
